#%PAM-1.0
# /etc/pam.d/dojo-lock-fingerprint  -- fingerprint ONLY (never falls through to a password prompt).
#
# pam_fprintd options worth setting (man pam_fprintd):
#   timeout=30    default 30 s; after this it returns PAM_AUTHINFO_UNAVAIL ("Verification timed out" TEXT_INFO,
#                 observed).  Use a finite value so the locker's worker re-arms (and re-claims the sensor) on a
#                 schedule it controls; timeout=-1 would hold the sensor claimed for the whole lock.
#   max-tries=3   default 3; after 3 no-matches it returns PAM_MAXTRIES.  The locker should then show
#                 "fingerprint disabled, use password" and NOT auto-restart until user activity / wake.
#                 (Keep this finite: it is the only brute-force limit on this path.)
# The locker must treat an immediate PAM_AUTHINFO_UNAVAIL (no enrolled print / no reader / fprintd missing)
# as "no fingerprint available" and not restart-loop.
#
# Deliberately NO pam_faillock here: a stranger's wrong finger must not lock the owner's account out of
# ly/sudo/password, and fprintd already bounds retries.  Fingerprint success also should not (and here does
# not) reset the password failure tally.
auth     required   pam_fprintd.so timeout=30 max-tries=3
# Locker only calls pam_authenticate(); account stanza only to keep pam_acct_mgmt harmless if ever called.
account  required   pam_permit.so
